                                "text": "To any man whom we have deprived or dispossessed of lands, castles, liberties, or rights, without the lawful judgement of his equals, we will at once restore these."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b55a490e-c127-4741-8b8b-a774d53eabc9",
                                "sense_id": "46614f2e-d6c4-3b29-b021-9b4372dab09d",
                                "text": "Whereupon the soldier dispossessed himself of his burden, and stood looking down upon it in great perplexity."
                            }
